From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: drive DSPP IGC and 3D gamut through LUTDMA

DPU 9.0 and later keep their color LUT blocks behind a LUT bus fed only
by the LUTDMA engine, with no memory-mapped write path, which is why
mainline exposes only PCC and GC on these SoCs. Port the engine from the
downstream sde driver (v2 layout for DPU 9.x, v3 for DPU 10.x and 12.x,
sideband queue, command buffers in the KMS VM) and use it for the DSPP
inverse gamma, exposed as a 256-entry DEGAMMA_LUT, and the 17^3 gamut
LUT, exposed as the CRTC blob property DPU_3D_LUT (drm_color_lut entries,
red fastest). The engine is mapped from an optional "lutdma" reg entry;
without it the properties are not exposed. A DSPP joins the topology only
on a modeset, so one is requested when color management starts or stops.

The LUT bus formats are not documented and were measured on hardware (by
feeding single-node inputs through the IGC and reading the interface CRC,
confirmed by eye with solid primaries): the IGC takes its three
components as (G, B, R), and the gamut block streams the 17^3 nodes in
drm_color_lut order (red fastest) with (R, G, B) per node, rotating
consecutive nodes through its four tables. The IGC has 257 samples at
i/256, so the 256-entry DEGAMMA_LUT is resampled onto it.

A command buffer is rewritten in place, so a DSPP update waits for the
previous transfer's done bit on every buffer it will touch before queuing
any of it, and skips the update if one is still pending; in-flight marks
are dropped on runtime resume, when the power domain has reset the status.

Verified on the AYN Odin 2 Portal (SM8550, engine v2) and Odin 3 (SM8750,
engine v3): transfers complete, the IGC and gamut registers read back
what the DMA wrote, and gamescope's shaper and 3D LUT scan out directly
with no DPU errors. SM8750's GC v2 is also a LUT bus block and is not
wired up.

